From 026f490f343fb026f3ac3f971e0ec45c00ac264c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:34:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] nv_attach: sum-map lookups inline, their adds on the
 global state space

A lookup of a sum map (1531) with a constant map fd becomes the calling
thread's shard address in the probe function (the trampoline's
sum_array_offset with the map's geometry and device copy as constants;
NULL without a copy), and a generic atomic whose address register only such
lookups define becomes atom/red .global on cvta.to.global of it. The copy is
device memory from cuMemAlloc, global memory by the programming guide, and a
generic address outside the const, local and shared windows maps to global
memory (PTX ISA 6.4.1.1). ptxas emits RED for such an add with its old value
unused; the generic atom was an ATOM.E whose returned predicate the thread
waited for. Hand-written shapes of this path on mul_mat_vec_q (results
gpu/probe-cost-20261117, section 7): the add from 0.061-0.069 to
0.010-0.015 ns per thread.

Other generic atomics keep the isspacep.local wrapper, now with an
isspacep.global branch before the generic form. The pass also runs without
thread-local maps (kernels are then not routed). The delivery's snapshot
kernel reads the copy through cvta.to.global + ld.relaxed.gpu.global, the
programs' form. Tests [sum-map-routing]; pt_victim's five tools exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
